    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27228" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭpīnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		lupus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a wolf, wolf's</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 3, 8, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 10, 20: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 19, 78, § 257</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>like a wolf</i>:
			impetus, Enn. ap. Don. <i><span class="en">Ter. Phorm. 2, 2, 25</span></i> (Sat. v. 28
			Vahl.): rictus, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2,
		98.</div>
